# SERENE — PROJECT BIBLE & CURSOR RULES
# Read this entire file before writing any code, proposing any structure, or making any architectural decision.
# This is the single source of truth for the Serene project.

---

## 1. WHAT SERENE IS

Serene is a wellness-first social media platform. It looks like Instagram on the surface — photos, videos, stories, profiles, follows — but its entire business logic, feed algorithm, AI layer, and design system are built around a completely different goal:

> Make users feel content, rested, and good about their lives — NOT maximise time on app.

This is not a marketing tagline. It is an engineering constraint. Every feature decision must be measured against it. If a feature would increase engagement at the cost of user wellbeing, the feature is wrong, not the measurement.

### What Serene is NOT
- Not an engagement-maximising platform
- Not ad-revenue driven in a traditional sense
- Not designed around follower counts, viral metrics, or social comparison
- Not infinite scroll by default
- Not a mental health app (it does not provide therapy or clinical support)

---

## 2. TECH STACK — USE EXACTLY THESE, NO SUBSTITUTIONS WITHOUT DISCUSSION

### Web App
- Framework: Next.js 14 (App Router, not Pages Router)
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode, no `any` types)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui for base components
- Animations: Framer Motion (gentle, never jarring)
- State: Zustand for global client state
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod validation

### Mobile App
- Framework: React Native with Expo SDK 51+
- Language: TypeScript
- Styling: NativeWind (Tailwind for React Native)
- Navigation: Expo Router (file-based, same mental model as Next.js)
- Animations: React Native Reanimated 3

### Backend & Infrastructure
- Database + Auth + Storage: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Edge Functions: Supabase Edge Functions (Deno/TypeScript)
- Media storage: Cloudflare R2 (images, videos)
- Video streaming: Cloudflare Stream
- Deployment (web): Vercel
- Deployment (backend): Supabase hosted

### AI Layer
- Primary model: Anthropic Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514)
- Use streaming responses for chat interfaces
- Never use OpenAI, Gemini, or any other provider without explicit discussion

### Analytics & Monitoring
- User analytics: Plausible (privacy-first, no fingerprinting, no user tracking across sites)
- Error monitoring: Sentry
- Never use Google Analytics, Mixpanel, or any tool that builds user profiles for ad targeting

